    "content": {
      "rendered": "<p>Hi there! I&#8217;m Raj Madhuram. I&#8217;m passionate about programming, technology, and education!</p>\n<p>Connect with me on LinkedIn:  <a href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/rmadhuram/\">https://www.linkedin.com/in/rmadhuram/</a></p>\n<p>In case you are wondering what the code &#8220;<span style=\"font-size: inherit; font-family: Raleway, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;\">68 65 6C 6C 6F 20 77 6F 72 6C 64 21&#8243; is about, it stands for &#8220;Hello World!&#8221; in ASCII. When someone learns to program, this message is the first thing they learn to output to screen. It is the first aha moment that leads to a life long journey into the fascinating world of computing!</span></p>\n<div class=\"col-6 col-sm-12\"> </div>\n\n\n<p></p>\n",
